# Git Workflow & Commit Conventions

## Multi-Repo Structure (CRITICAL)

Each app is a **separate git repository**. The workspace root has its own repo for rules/config.

```
Resmo/                    # Workspace repo (rules, root config)
├── .cursor/rules/        # Committed here
├── package.json          # Workspace config
└── apps/                 # IGNORED in workspace repo
    ├── backend/          # Separate git repo → github.com/.../resmo-backend
    ├── superadmin/       # Separate git repo → github.com/.../resmo-superadmin
    ├── company/          # Separate git repo → github.com/.../resmo-company
    ├── admin/            # Separate git repo → github.com/.../resmo-admin
    └── consillier/       # Separate git repo → github.com/.../resmo-consillier
```

## Which Repo to Commit To?

| Changed Files | Commit To | Working Directory |
|--------------|-----------|-------------------|
| `apps/backend/*` | backend repo | `apps/backend` |
| `apps/superadmin/*` | superadmin repo | `apps/superadmin` |
| `apps/company/*` | company repo | `apps/company` |
| `apps/admin/*` | admin repo | `apps/admin` |
| `apps/consillier/*` | consillier repo | `apps/consillier` |
| `.cursor/rules/*` | workspace root repo | Workspace root |
| `package.json` (root) | workspace root repo | Workspace root |

**NEVER** commit from workspace root expecting app changes to be included.

## Cross-App Features
When a feature spans multiple apps:
1. Commit backend changes first -> push
2. Commit frontend changes -> push
3. Use same commit message prefix for traceability

## Commit Message Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[optional body - what and why, not how]
```

### Types

| Type | When to Use |
|------|-------------|
| `feat` | New feature or capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Code change that neither fixes nor adds |
| `chore` | Dependencies, config, build changes |
| `style` | Formatting only (no logic change) |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `test` | Adding or updating tests |

### Scopes

| Scope | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `backend` | API, controllers, models |
| `superadmin` | Superadmin dashboard |
| `company` | Company dashboard |
| `admin` | Admin dashboard |
| `conseiller` | Conseiller dashboard |
| `ui` | Shared components |
| `i18n` | Translations |
| `auth` | Authentication |
| `db` | Database schemas/migrations |

### Examples
```bash
feat(superadmin): add country and category to company management
fix(backend): handle expired JWT tokens gracefully
feat(ui,i18n): add searchable combobox with RTL support
feat(api)!: change company response structure  # breaking change
```

### Rules
- Subject: max 72 chars, imperative mood, no period
- Body: explain WHAT changed and WHY (not how)
- Reference issues: `Fixes #123` or `Closes #456`
